    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d544">

                <pb facs="0737" n="725" xml:id="pg725"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.248/2–645: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Spain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Butterworth</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-02-06T21:00:00+01:00">February 6, 1945—9
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 7—11:02 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>276. For Hickerson<anchor n="81" xml:id="d544-f1"/> and Culbertson.<anchor n="82"
                        xml:id="d544-f2"/> After several meetings attended by George, Payne, Haering
                    and Bond with the Spanish delegation the following definite proposal was finally
                    obtained from the Spanish Government. As translated it reads:</p>
                <p>[Here follows text as in protocol effected by exchange of notes, February 19,
                    printed on <ref target="#pg727">pages 727</ref>–<ref target="#pg730">730</ref>,
                    except that in final text article V was added and articles V to XI of this draft
                    were accordingly renumbered.]</p>
                <p>Pertinent comment will follow.</p>
                <p>George and Payne left for Lisbon tonight.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Butterworth</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d544-f1" n="81" xml:id="d544-f1-content">
                <p>John D, Hickerson, Deputy Director, Office of European Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d544-f2" n="82" xml:id="d544-f2-content">
                <p>Paul T, Culbertson, Chief, Division of Western European Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
